<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to Nov 23.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to Nov 23.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to Nov 23 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week Nov 17-Nov 23</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97	 179,499 tns	 13,313 tns     7.42 pct</p>
<p>     95-96	 430,416 tns	 32,414 tns     7.53 pct</p>
<p>     94-95	 285,359 tns	 23,212 tns     8.13 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to Nov 23</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97	 302,116 tns	 21,905 tns     7.25 pct</p>
<p>     95-96	 806,736 tns	 57,771 tns     7.16 pct</p>
<p>     94-95	 487,613 tns	 35,968 tns     7.38 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 12 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 21 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 10 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 728-9530</p>
